From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <pviano@riasolutionsgroup.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix nullable reference warnings in the generated library

Annotate the generated library so it builds warning-free under
<Nullable>enable</Nullable> without suppressing any nullable diagnostics:
- events made nullable (never = null!);
- members genuinely used as nullable (SortColumn, Widget?, IDataObject.GetData,
  ControlUtility results, PaintEventArgs consumers) given proper ? annotations;
- framework-initialized auto-properties/fields kept at their WinForms-compatible
  non-null types via = null! only where the value is set post-construction;
- targeted null-guards / null-forgiving at deref/return/argument sites.

Applied after generation by GitPatchApplier (git apply --3way).
---
